<title>UK: U.S.'s KKR eyes Littlewoods shops - paper.</title>
<headline>U.S.'s KKR eyes Littlewoods shops - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. buyout specialist Kohlberg Kravis Roberts (KKR) has offered to buy the 135 shops put up for sale by private company Littlewoods for around 450 million stg ($722.5 million), a British newspaper said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The Independent on Sunday said KKR and Littlewoods executives had held talks about a possible sale.</p>
<p>Last week, Littlewoods said it wanted to sell the stores to focus on its mail order and football pools leisure businesses.</p>
<p>Food retailer Tesco Plc and value-for-money ASDA Group Plc were tipped as possible buyers.</p>
<p>($1=.6228 Stg)</p>
